<BaseLayout title="Privacy information | Best Letting Agent for Landlords" description="How Loud Crowd IT Ltd handles website connection data, postcode comparisons and privacy requests on this independent landlord guide, with contact details." canonicalPath="/privacy/">
 <SiteHeader />
 <main class="section-shell prose" style="padding-block:3rem;max-width:52rem">
  <h1>Privacy information</h1><p>Updated 24 October 2026.</p>
  <p>Loud Crowd IT Ltd (10278925), 3 Railway Court, Doncaster DN4 5FB, publishes this independent guide. We are not a letting agency. Contact <a href="mailto:david@loudcrowd.agency">david@loudcrowd.agency</a> about privacy.</p>
  <h2>Guide and comparison tool</h2>
  <p>The postcode comparison uses the postcode and service in the page URL to show an area guide. It does not submit a landlord enquiry or transfer your details to an agent. Avoid adding personal details to a URL. Cloudflare processes connection data and requested URLs to host and protect the site. Google Fonts receives connection information when your browser loads fonts.</p>
  <h2>Recommendation submissions</h2>
  <p>Recommendation collection is paused pending storage, notification, privacy and mailbox checks. It is separate from an enquiry about letting your property. No current Doncaster referral arrangement is offered.</p>
  <h2>Email and external links</h2>
  <p>If you email the publisher, we use the information to answer your request under our legitimate interest in responding. Please do not include tenant details. We do not add you to marketing or forward your details to an agent. We review correspondence for deletion within 90 days unless a separate relationship or legal requirement needs a different period.</p>
  <p>Links to the Doncaster fee guide open another LoudCrowd publication. External sites process information under their own notices. A link or telephone-button click is not evidence of a completed call or referral.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2><p>You can ask for access, correction or deletion, or object to processing, using the contact above. Rights depend on the circumstances. You may complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p>
 </main><SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
